Coordinates `x = (v, r, θ, φ)` (`x 0 = v`, `x 1 = r`, `x 2 = θ`, `x 3 = φ`), signature `(-,+,+,+)`.
Two **independent** real parameters enter the metric (`M`, `b`); the electromagnetic data carry the charge
`Q`. Nothing here sets `b = Q²`: that relation is *derived* (`EF.einsteinMaxwell_eq`, `EF.cert_iff`).

* `fRN M b r = 1 - 2M/r + b/r²`;
* `gRN M b = -f_b dv² + 2 dv dr + r² (dθ² + sin²θ dφ²)` (so `g_{vr} = g_{rv} = 1`, half of the cross term);
* `giRN M b`: candidate inverse `[[0,1,0,0],[1,f_b,0,0],[0,0,r⁻²,0],[0,0,0,(r² sin²θ)⁻¹]]`, certified
  separately (never assumed);
* `emPotentialRN Q = -(Q/r) dv` (written `-Q / r`), `faradayRN Q`: `F_{rv} = Q/r²`, `F_{vr} = -Q/r²`,
